; The posts' collision and structural extent is the full 3.9 m below, but their
; top 0.5 m sits entirely inside the header's solid, where nothing has ever been
; visible. While both were raw boxes their coincident top and side faces were
; hidden by depth; once both are chamfered the two rolled corners interpenetrate
; at a grazing angle inside the header and the junction self-shadows into a band
; of acne at eye level. The visible post therefore stops 0.05 m into the header
; instead of running through it. Shape_frame_post below is unchanged: this moves
; a hidden render surface, not a collidable one.
[sub_resource type="BoxMesh" id="Mesh_frame_post"]
material = SubResource("Material_frame")
size = Vector3(0.5, 3.45, 0.72)

[sub_resource type="BoxMesh" id="Mesh_frame_header"]
material = SubResource("Material_trim")
size = Vector3(4.2, 0.5, 0.72)

